[ar:ARK Music]
[ti:Velvet Teeth]
[al:Problem's]

[00:02.59]Smile for the picture,
[00:04.37]Straighten your sleeve,
[00:06.79]Nobody notices
[00:09.07]What you don't leave.
[00:11.75]Light in the hallway,
[00:13.62]Lock on the door,
[00:16.16]Someone says “nothing,”
[00:17.76]Someone says more.
[00:21.15]Little white secrets in little white rooms,
[00:23.12]Flowers grow crooked when nobody moves,
[00:25.50]Hands in the pockets, eyes on the floor,
[00:27.75]Laugh like you never needed anything more.
[00:30.18]A whisper gets carried, a rumor gets dressed,
[00:32.36]A stranger gets blamed for the weight in your chest,
[00:34.71]Everybody's talking, nobody hears,
[00:37.11]A hundred small echoes become bigger than fear.
[00:39.44]And the night keeps turning,
[00:41.16]The red light burning,
[00:42.31]Someone's looking over their shoulder again,
[00:44.54]One word gets twisted,
[00:45.75]One heart gets lifted,
[00:46.84]One heart gets broken pretending it's fine.
[00:49.37]Velvet teeth, velvet teeth,
[00:51.07]Soft when they smile, sharp underneath,
[00:53.25]Dancing on glass with a beautiful beat,
[00:55.56]Nobody sees what's hiding beneath.
[00:58.08]Velvet teeth, velvet teeth,
[01:00.41]Sweet little lies with a bitter belief,
[01:02.98]Hold me close, then pull away,
[01:05.10]Love can look different when it's afraid.
[01:08.32]Na-na, keep the rhythm alive,
[01:10.42]Na-na, keep the smile in line,
[01:13.06]Na-na, nobody needs to know,
[01:15.24]How deep the little shadows go.
[01:17.31]Someone gets louder when someone's afraid,
[01:19.67]Someone gets colder to cover the shade,
[01:22.32]Someone says “hate” when they wanted “don't leave,”
[01:24.42]Someone breaks hearts just to prove they can breathe.
[01:26.87]A room full of people, a world full of eyes,
[01:29.13]Everybody wearing somebody else's disguise,
[01:31.61]One person's silence becomes another's blame,
[01:33.67]Then everybody walks home carrying the same.
[01:35.90]And the wheels keep spinning,
[01:37.40]The old game winning,
[01:38.53]Round and around till the morning turns blue,
[01:40.68]Nobody started
[01:41.75]With wanting to hurt it,
[01:43.11]But somebody always finds something to lose.
[01:45.56]Velvet teeth, velvet teeth,
[01:47.02]Soft when they smile, sharp underneath,
[01:49.59]Dancing on glass with a beautiful beat,
[01:51.72]Nobody sees what's hiding beneath.
[01:54.20]Velvet teeth, velvet teeth,
[01:56.47]Sweet little lies with a bitter belief,
[01:59.02]Hold me close, then pull away,
[02:01.44]Love can look different when it's afraid.
[02:04.22]There was a child
[02:08.16]Who learned to stay small,
[02:09.57]A voice in the doorway
[02:12.08]That learned not to call.
[02:14.52]There was a heart
[02:16.88]That was scared to be seen,
[02:19.32]So it painted its colors
[02:21.01]The safest of green.
[02:22.94]There was a hand
[02:24.17]That could've reached out,
[02:25.35]But pride built a wall
[02:26.50]Where love had been found.
[02:27.70]And somewhere between
[02:28.83]The “never again”
[02:29.98]And “I'll get you first,”
[02:32.32]We became strangers again.
[02:34.74]Don't turn away,
[02:35.72]Don't turn away,
[02:36.88]Don't turn away from the face in the frame.
[02:39.38]Don't pass it on,
[02:40.45]Don't pass it on,
[02:41.53]Don't pass the fire and call it a game.
[02:43.95]Don't make a weapon
[02:45.16]Out of your pain,
[02:46.33]Don't make a prison
[02:47.48]Out of somebody's name.
[02:52.82]Velvet teeth, velvet teeth,
[02:54.38]Soft when they smile, sharp underneath,
[02:56.63]Dancing on glass with a beautiful beat,
[02:59.35]Everybody hides something underneath.
[03:02.05]Velvet teeth, velvet teeth,
[03:03.89]Hearts learn to run before they learn to speak,
[03:06.06]Hold me close, don't turn away,
[03:08.54]Maybe we're both just afraid.
[03:11.85]Velvet teeth, velvet teeth,
[03:13.05]All of the damage we never repeat,
[03:15.92]If the world keeps teaching us
[03:17.48]Love has to bleed,
[03:18.37]Then maybe we change
[03:19.50]What we're teaching the next.
[03:20.77]Smile for the picture,
[03:23.63]Straighten your sleeve,
[03:26.15]Some things get lighter
[03:28.12]When we let them be seen.
[03:30.33]Light in the hallway,
[03:33.02]Lock on the door...
[03:35.56]Someone says “nothing.”
[03:38.48]Someone finally says,
[03:41.38]“I'm scared.”